## Context

A digital learning platform for the Cimory Group and Kanzler sales teams that evolved into a broader Learning Management System initiative.

## Problem

TODO(content): what the sales training process lacked before the platform (IN-05).

## My role

Owner: I translated the HR and sales-training needs into features and built the platform. As the scope expanded, it was handed over to the IT team for further development and production deployment.

## As-is analysis

TODO(content): how sales training worked before (IN-05).

## Requirements

- Video modules with viewing-progress validation, chapter quizzes, XP, badges and leaderboards.
- A content management system with Excel bulk import, so HR can manage learning content without code changes.
- Authentication, content protection and performance testing.

## Solution design

The backend started with Express.js. As the scope grew, I developed a hybrid architecture with Express.js and NestJS using the Strangler Pattern, so selected components could migrate step by step without rewriting the whole backend. Learning videos are stored in Cloudflare R2 object storage, separate from the application server.

## Build

Node.js, Express, NestJS, PostgreSQL, Cloudflare R2 and permission-based Power BI reporting.

## Verification

Seven k6 test scenarios: smoke, load, stress, spike, soak, database benchmarking and object storage benchmarking.

## Outcome

0.17% errors at 1,000 virtual users in the stress test and 0.01% errors in a 1-hour soak test. The project was handed over to IT for production deployment.

